claim.claim-text:
an input preparation module that accesses a sequence database and generates
(i) a reference sequence that contains, at a target position, a base, wherein the reference sequence is a promoter sequence of a gene, and
(ii) an alternative base sequence that contains, at the target position, a variant of the base;

a sequence-to-sequence model that
processes the reference sequence and generates a reference output, wherein the reference output specifies, for each base in the reference sequence, signal levels of a plurality of epigenetic tracks, and
processes the alternative sequence and generates an alternative output, wherein the alternative output specifies, for each base in the alternative sequence, the signal levels of the plurality of epigenetic tracks;

accessing a sequence database and generating
(i) a reference sequence that contains, at a target position, a base, wherein the reference sequence is a promoter sequence of a gene, and
(ii) an alternative base sequence that contains, at the target position, a variant of the base;

accessing a sequence database and generating
(i) a reference sequence that contains, at a target position, a base, wherein the reference sequence is a non-coding sequence, and
(ii) an alternative base sequence that contains, at the target position, a variant of the base;
